{
    "overview": "Fix the confirmation/review mechanism in the SE3 workflow engine to properly handle human review at propose and design phases. The fix addresses three core issues: (1) incorrect status checking logic that looks for approved=false instead of approved=true for successful confirmations, (2) improper revision transition setup when human requests changes, and (3) missing logic to check for existing call file responses on resume. The solution ensures that when confirmation is enabled in se3.yaml, the flow correctly pauses after propose/design steps, waits for human approval, and properly resumes after receiving a response.",
    "architecture_decisions": [
        {
            "decision": "Separate status return values for CONFIRM step based on human response",
            "rationale": "The confirm handler currently returns PAUSED status regardless of whether human approved or rejected. This causes the state machine to treat approved confirmations as still waiting. We need to return COMPLETED when approved=true so the state machine transitions normally, and a distinct status when changes are requested to trigger revision.",
            "alternatives_considered": "Alternative was to keep PAUSED status and change state machine logic to check call file response directly, but this couples the state machine too tightly to call file internals. Keeping status semantics clear (COMPLETED=proceed, REVISION_NEEDED=go back) is cleaner."
        },
        {
            "decision": "Add revision transition path in state machine for CONFIRM steps",
            "rationale": "When human requests changes, we need to transition back to the previous step (propose or design) for revision rather than moving forward. This requires the state machine to recognize a new transition type from CONFIRM steps.",
            "alternatives_considered": "Alternative was to use the existing retry/rollback mechanism, but CONFIRM revisions have unique semantics - we need to preserve the original step context while triggering a revision loop that will come back to CONFIRM after revision."
        },
        {
            "decision": "Check for existing responses in confirm handler on resume",
            "rationale": "When resuming a PAUSED flow at a CONFIRM step, the handler needs to first check if a response file already exists (human already responded) before creating a new call file. This prevents duplicate call files and enables immediate continuation.",
            "alternatives_considered": "Alternative was to handle this in run.py before calling the step handler, but that would require run.py to know about call file internals. Better to encapsulate this logic within the confirm step handler itself."
        },
        {
            "decision": "Use REVISION_NEEDED status to signal backward transition",
            "rationale": "Introduce a new step status REVISION_NEEDED that the state machine recognizes as a signal to transition backward to the previous step rather than forward. This makes the intent explicit in the state machine transition logic.",
            "alternatives_considered": "Alternative was to overload FAILED status with revision metadata, but that conflates failure (error occurred) with revision (human wants changes). Explicit status is clearer."
        }
    ],
    "components": [
        {
            "name": "StateMachine",
            "responsibilities": "Manage flow state transitions, handle CONFIRM step special cases, properly route approved confirmations forward and revision requests backward. Fix _insert_confirmation_steps to pass project_root, fix transition_to_next to handle CONFIRM outcomes correctly.",
            "interfaces": "transition_to_next(current_step, step_result) -> next_step, _transition_to_revision(step, reason) -> prev_step, _insert_confirmation_steps(workflow_steps, config) -> steps_with_confirm"
        },
        {
            "name": "ConfirmStepHandler",
            "responsibilities": "Handle CONFIRM step execution - check for existing responses on resume, create call files for human review, wait for responses, return appropriate status (COMPLETED for approval, REVISION_NEEDED for changes). Update _trigger_revision to properly signal state machine.",
            "interfaces": "confirm_handler(context) -> StepStatus, _check_existing_response(call_file_path) -> Response|None, _wait_for_human_response(call_file_path, timeout) -> Response, _trigger_revision(context, feedback) -> None"
        },
        {
            "name": "RunCommand",
            "responsibilities": "Orchestrate flow execution, handle resume logic specially for CONFIRM steps by pre-checking response files before invoking handler, ensure proper flow continuation after confirmation approval.",
            "interfaces": "run(resume=False), _execute_step(step, context), _should_skip_confirm_step(step, state) -> bool"
        },
        {
            "name": "CallFileManager",
            "responsibilities": "Manage human call file lifecycle - create call files, check for responses, parse response content. Used by confirm handler for async human communication.",
            "interfaces": "create_call(step, context) -> path, check_response(path) -> Response|None, parse_response(path) -> Response"
        }
    ],
    "data_flow": "1. On normal flow: StateMachine inserts CONFIRM steps after propose/design -> Flow executes propose step -> Enters CONFIRM step -> ConfirmHandler creates call file -> Returns PAUSED -> RunCommand saves state and exits. 2. On resume: RunCommand detects CONFIRM step -> ConfirmHandler checks for existing response -> If approved: returns COMPLETED -> StateMachine transitions to next step. If changes requested: returns REVISION_NEEDED -> StateMachine transitions back to propose/design -> After revision completes, returns to CONFIRM again. 3. Response file format contains approved boolean and optional feedback text, parsed by CallFileManager.",
    "implementation_plan": [
        "Step 1: Fix _insert_confirmation_steps in state_machine.py to properly pass project_root to load_confirmation_config",
        "Step 2: Add REVISION_NEEDED to StepStatus enum if not exists",
        "Step 3: Update transition_to_next in state_machine.py to handle CONFIRM step results - approved=true transitions forward, approved=false triggers revision transition",
        "Step 4: Implement _transition_to_revision method in state_machine.py to route back to previous step (propose or design)",
        "Step 5: Update confirm.py confirm_handler to return COMPLETED after successful human approval instead of PAUSED",
        "Step 6: Fix _trigger_revision in confirm.py to properly signal REVISION_NEEDED status",
        "Step 7: Update _wait_for_human_response in confirm.py for more robust file watching with timeout handling",
        "Step 8: Add _check_existing_response logic in confirm.py to detect already-answered calls on resume",
        "Step 9: Update run.py to add special handling for CONFIRM steps when resuming - check if call file already has response before invoking handler",
        "Step 10: Ensure run.py properly continues flow after confirmation approval by checking step result status",
        "Step 11: Add tests for confirmation flow scenarios: approve, request changes, resume with existing response",
        "Step 12: Run full test suite to verify no regressions"
    ],
    "testing_strategy": "Unit tests for each fixed component: (1) Test state_machine transition logic with mocked CONFIRM results - verify approved=true goes forward, approved=false goes to revision. (2) Test confirm handler with mocked call files - verify returns COMPLETED on approval, REVISION_NEEDED on changes. (3) Test resume logic in run.py - verify skips creating new call file when response exists. Integration test: Configure se3.yaml with confirmation for propose, run through full flow verifying pause, response, and resume behavior. Edge cases: timeout handling, missing call files, malformed responses."
}
